verses.text:
and the eternal God will tread upon the earth, on Mount Sinai.{e}
He will appear with his host,{f}
and appear in the strength of his might from the highest heaven.

The high mountains will be shaken;
the lofty hills will be brought low
and will melt like wax before a flame.

The earth will be split wide apart,{h}
and everything on the earth will perish,
and there will be judgment upon all.

But with the righteous he will make peace;
he will guard the chosen,
and mercy will rest upon them.
They will all belong to God;
he will grant them his favor
and bless them all.
He will help them all;
light will shine upon them,
and he will make peace with them.

Look, he comes with myriads of his holy ones,{i}
to execute judgment upon all,
to destroy all the wicked,
and to convict all flesh
for all the works of their wickedness that they have wickedly done,
and for all the proud and harsh words that wicked sinners have spoken against him.

In those days you will make your names an everlasting curse for all the righteous;
by you all who curse will curse,
and all the sinners and the godless will swear by you.
For you, the godless, there will be a curse.
But all the righteous will rejoice;{a}
there will be forgiveness of sins,
and every mercy and peace and kindness.
There will be salvation for them, a good light.
But for all of you sinners there will be no salvation;
a curse will rest upon you all.

Those who never sleep bless you. They stand before your glory and bless, praise, and exalt you, saying:
‘Holy, holy, holy is the Lord of Spirits;
he fills the earth with spirits.’ ”{d}

Wisdom went out to make her home among human beings,
but found no home;
so Wisdom went back to her place
and took her seat among the angels.{a}

On that day my Chosen One will sit on the throne of glory,
and will choose among their deeds,{a}
and their resting places will be past counting;
their spirits will grow strong within them when they see my chosen ones
and those who have called on my holy and glorious name.

Then I will make my Chosen One live among them;
I will transform heaven
and make it an everlasting blessing and light.

I will transform the dry ground and make it a blessing,
and I will make my chosen ones live on it;
but sinners and evildoers will not set foot on it.{b}

He answered me,
“This is the Son of Man who has righteousness,
with whom righteousness lives,
who will reveal all the treasures of what is hidden;
for the Lord of Spirits has chosen him,
and his lot has prevailed before the Lord of Spirits in uprightness forever.

These are the ones who judge the stars of heaven,{c}
who raise their hands against the Most High,
who tread the dry ground and live on it.
All their deeds show wrongdoing,
and their deeds are wrongdoing;{d}
their strength rests on their wealth,
and their trust is in the gods their own hands have made;
they deny the name of the Lord of Spirits.

In those days I watched the Head of Days sit down on his glorious throne;
the books of the living lay open before him,
and his whole host in the heavens above and his council stood before him.{b}

Even before the sun and the constellations were created,
before the stars of heaven were made,
his name was spoken before the Lord of Spirits.{a}

He will be a staff for the righteous,
to lean on so that they do not fall;
he will be the light of the nations
and the hope of those who grieve in their hearts.{b}

The wisdom of the Lord of Spirits has revealed him to the holy and the righteous,
for he guards the portion of the just,
since they loathed and spurned this world of wrongdoing
and detested all that is done in it and all its ways, in the Lord of Spirits’ name.
By his name they find salvation,
and he is the one who will avenge their lives.{c}

In those days the kings of the earth will be downcast,
and the strong who hold the dry ground, because of the deeds of their hands;
for on the day of their anguish and distress they will not save themselves.

For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness,
and wrongdoing will pass away like a shadow
and will have no standing;
for the Chosen One has taken his stand before the Lord of Spirits,
and his glory is forever and ever,
and his power for all generations.

He will judge hidden things,
and no one will be able to speak an empty word in his presence;
for he is the Chosen One before the Lord of Spirits, as he wills.

He is righteous in his judgment,
and in the presence of his glory wrongdoing will not stand;
at his judgment whoever does not repent will perish before him.

In those days the earth will hand back what was entrusted to it,
Sheol will hand back what it has received,
and destruction will repay what it owes.{a}

In those days the Chosen One will sit on my throne,{c}
and from his mouth will pour every secret of wisdom and counsel,
for the Lord of Spirits has granted them to him and glorified him.

In those days the mountains will bound like rams,
the hills will leap like lambs that have had their fill of milk,{d}
and the faces of all the angels in heaven will glow with joy.

Their hands commit lawless acts;
whatever the righteous toil for, the sinners devour in their lawlessness.{a}
But the sinners will be destroyed before the Lord of Spirits,
banished from his earth,
and they will perish forever and ever.

These mountains will not stand firm like the earth before his righteousness;{c}
the hills will become like a spring of water;
and the righteous will have rest from the harassment of sinners.”

Then that valley will be filled with their chosen and beloved ones;
the days of their lives will be over,
and the days of their leading others astray will no longer be counted.

In those days the angels will gather
and launch themselves eastward against the Parthians and Medes.{b}
They will stir up the kings, so that a spirit of turmoil comes over them;
they will shake them from their thrones,
and they will burst out like lions from their dens
and like starving wolves among the flocks.

But the city of my righteous ones will be an obstacle to their horses.{c}
They will start fighting each other;
their own right hands will be strong against them;
a man will not acknowledge his brother,
nor a son his father or his mother,
until the corpses from their slaughter are past counting,
and their punishment will not be in vain.

After this the holy ones in heaven will be told
to search out the secrets of righteousness, the inheritance of faith;
for it has risen like the sun on the dry ground,
and darkness has gone by.

The chosen will begin to live with the chosen;
these are the measurements that will be given to faith
and will make righteousness firm.

The Lord of Spirits placed the Chosen One on the throne of glory,{b}
and he will judge all the works of the holy ones in heaven above,
and weigh their deeds in the scales.

All in heaven above who never sleep will bless him;
every holy one in heaven will bless him,
and all the chosen who live in the garden of life,
and every spirit of light that can bless, glorify, exalt, and hallow your blessed name;
and all flesh will glorify and bless your name beyond all measure, forever and ever.

One group of them will look at the other;
they will be terrified,
their faces will fall,
and pain will grip them
when they see that Son of a Woman{d}
seated on his glorious throne.

For from the start the Son of Man was hidden;
the Most High kept him in the presence of his power
and revealed him to the chosen.

The Lord of Spirits will live over them;
with that Son of Man they will eat,
lie down, and rise, forever and ever.

By that oath the sea was created,
and for its foundation he set the sand against the time of its fury,
and it dares not go beyond it, from the creation of the world and forever.{g}

By that oath the stars complete their courses;
he summons each by name,
and they reply to him, from age to age.{h}

This oath is strong over them;
by it they are kept, their paths are kept,
and their course is not destroyed.

There was great joy among them;
they blessed, glorified, and exalted,
because the name of that Son of Man had been revealed to them.

After this my spirit was taken away
and went up into the heavens.
I saw the children of God{a}
stepping on flames of fire;
their garments were white,
and their faces shone like snow.

I saw two rivers of fire,
whose fire gleamed like hyacinth,{b}
and I threw myself face down before the Lord of Spirits.

The angel Michael, one of the archangels, took me by my right hand,
lifted me up, and led me out into all the secrets;
he showed me all the secrets of mercy and of righteousness.

He carried my spirit off into the heaven of heavens,
and there I saw something like a structure built of crystals,{c}
and between the crystals tongues of living fire.

My spirit saw a ring of fire encircling that house;
on its four sides were rivers full of living fire,
and they encircled that house.

Around it were seraphim, cherubim, and ophanim;
these are the ones who never sleep
and who guard the throne of his glory.
